# 21. Emerging National Conservation Architecture

The project can now begin assembling a common conservation-performance architecture.

## Layer 1 — Know

Monitor ecological condition.

## Layer 2 — Diagnose

Identify pressures and limiting factors.

## Layer 3 — Decide

Match authorities, resources, and objectives.

## Layer 4 — Act

Implement interventions.

## Layer 5 — Measure

Determine physical and biological response.

## Layer 6 — Learn

Evaluate effectiveness and uncertainty.

## Layer 7 — Adapt

Modify management where evidence warrants.

## Layer 8 — Maintain

Protect gains over time.

Simplified:

> **KNOW → DIAGNOSE → DECIDE → ACT → MEASURE → LEARN → ADAPT → MAINTAIN**

This is becoming the project's central institutional-performance model.

